§§ `109(ב), 110, 111 — ההפניות בפרק סגני המנהלים הראשונים שאינם אקדמאים`

-- This copy's §109(ב) applies "סעיף 71(ג)", its §110 "סעיף 72" and its
-- §111 "סעיף 67": the principals' sections, the very three §§80(ב), 81 and
-- 82 apply to a non-academic principal. The primary prints 98(ג), 99 and 93,
-- the first deputies' own. The chapter is the first deputies' (§107 converts
-- them "by the rules of an academic first deputy"), so each is read as the
-- primary prints it (convention reading.misprint) — as the primary's
-- encoding reads §108's "סעיף 70" as §97 (F-ofek-hadash-base-108-a), the
-- one reference both copies print the principals' way. The two copies of
-- one instrument disagree: F-ofek-hadash-base-registry-copy-a.
--
-- §109(ב) as read is §98(ג): a first deputy whose A passes the top grade of
-- his school's level is placed at grade 4 of the first deputies' table — the
-- primary's `a non-academic first deputy's placement` (base-agreement-109),
-- the row's last cell. As printed, §71(ג) would place him "בטבלת השכר
-- המשולב למנהלים בדרגה 4", on the principals' table. §110 and §111 follow.
@ref akn:art_109__para_b akn:art_110/p1 akn:art_111/p1
DECLARE `cross-reference as the two copies print it` HAS
    `the clause that refers`        IS A STRING
    `the section this copy cites`   IS A STRING
    `the section the primary cites` IS A STRING

GIVEN clause IS A STRING, `this copy` IS A STRING, `the primary` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `cross-reference as the two copies print it`
DECIDE `printed in the two copies as` clause `this copy` `the primary` IS
    `cross-reference as the two copies print it` WITH
        `the clause that refers`        IS clause
        `the section this copy cites`   IS `this copy`
        `the section the primary cites` IS `the primary`

`the references of §§109 to 111 in the two copies` MEANS LIST
    `printed in the two copies as` "109(ב)" "71(ג)" "98(ג)",
    `printed in the two copies as` "110" "72" "99",
    `printed in the two copies as` "111" "67" "93"

-- What §§80(ב), 81 and 82 apply to a non-academic principal, in both copies.
`the sections §§80(ב), 81 and 82 cite` MEANS LIST "71(ג)", "72", "67"

GIVEN r IS A `cross-reference as the two copies print it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the two copies differ in` r IF
    NOT (r's `the section this copy cites` EQUALS r's `the section the primary cites`)

`this copy's §§109 to 111 cite the principals' sections` MEANS
        all `the two copies differ in` `the references of §§109 to 111 in the two copies`
    AND (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the section this copy cites`) `the references of §§109 to 111 in the two copies`) EQUALS `the sections §§80(ב), 81 and 82 cite`

#ASSERT `this copy's §§109 to 111 cite the principals' sections`

-- §110 as read: a non-academic first deputy's personal supplement on §99's
-- terms, Y being the first deputies' 20%. As printed ("סעיף 72") it would
-- be the principal's, on Y of 15%: money turns on the difference.
GIVEN t IS A NUMBER, `new table pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a non-academic first deputy's supplement rate, as this copy's §110 is read` t `new table pay` IS
    `a non-academic first deputy's supplement rate` t `new table pay`

GIVEN t IS A NUMBER, `new table pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a non-academic first deputy's supplement rate, as this copy's §110 is printed` t `new table pay` IS
    `a non-academic principal's supplement rate` t `new table pay`

-- T of 12,000 and a new table salary of 13,000: B is 13,920 by §99's Y,
-- 13,440 by §72's — a supplement of 920 or 440 a month.
#ASSERT `a non-academic first deputy's supplement rate, as this copy's §110 is read` 12000 13000 TIMES 13000 EQUALS 920
#ASSERT `a non-academic first deputy's supplement rate, as this copy's §110 is printed` 12000 13000 TIMES 13000 EQUALS 440

-- §111 as read (§93) and as printed (§67) compute alike: §93 applies §67 to
-- a first deputy, so no amount turns on this one.
GIVEN `supplement in each year so far` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the new level's supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a non-academic first deputy's supplement after a fall, as this copy's §111 is read` `supplement in each year so far` `the new level's supplement` IS
    `a non-academic first deputy's supplement after a fall` `supplement in each year so far` `the new level's supplement`

#ASSERT (    `a non-academic first deputy's supplement after a fall, as this copy's §111 is read` (LIST 2436, 2436, 2436, 2436) 1218
         EQUALS `a non-academic principal's supplement after a fall` (LIST 2436, 2436, 2436, 2436) 1218)

