§§ `בדיקת טבלאות השכר`

-- The checks: what the primary says of each table, and what each table's
-- own header and rows print, run over every cell. A cell is named by its
-- row's label and its grade; a figure is set beside a cell rounded to the
-- agora (convention rounding.half).

`this copy's teachers' salary tables` MEANS LIST
    `this copy's annex ו'`, `this copy's annex ז'`, `this copy's annex ד'`, `this copy's annex ה'`,
    `this copy's annex ט'`, `this copy's annex י'`, `this copy's annex י"א`

`this copy's academic principals' tables` MEANS LIST `this copy's annex י"ב`, `this copy's annex י"ג`

`this copy's other principals' and deputies' tables` MEANS LIST
    `this copy's annex י"ד`, `this copy's annex ט"ו`, `this copy's annex ט"ז`,
    `this copy's annex י"ז`, `this copy's annex י"ח`,
    `this copy's annex י"ט`, `this copy's annex כ'`, `this copy's annex כ"א`

`this copy's principals' and deputies' tables` MEANS
    append `this copy's academic principals' tables` `this copy's other principals' and deputies' tables`

@desc A cell of a salary table of this copy, by its row's label and its grade.
DECLARE `annexed cell` HAS
    `the cell's label` IS A NUMBER
    `the cell's grade` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN l IS A NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `annexed cell`
DECIDE `the annexed cell at` l g IS
    `annexed cell` WITH
        `the cell's label` IS l
        `the cell's grade` IS g

-- The cells a table prints otherwise than a figure for each label and
-- grade; and the cells one table prints that another prints otherwise at
-- the same label and grade.
GIVEN t IS AN `annexed pay table`, f IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER AND NUMBER TO NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `annexed cell`
DECIDE `the cells printed otherwise than` t f IS
    concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD
                     map (GIVEN c YIELD `the annexed cell at` (r's `the row's label`) (c's grade))
                         (filter (GIVEN c YIELD NOT (c's pay EQUALS `to the agora` (f (r's `the row's label`) (c's grade))))
                                 (r's `the row's cells`)))
                (t's `annexed pay table's rows`))

GIVEN a IS AN `annexed pay table`, b IS AN `annexed pay table`
GIVETH A LIST OF `annexed cell`
DECIDE `the cells one table prints otherwise than the other` a b IS
    concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD
                     map (GIVEN c YIELD `the annexed cell at` (r's `the row's label`) (c's grade))
                         (filter (GIVEN c YIELD NOT (`the annexed pay at` b (r's `the row's label`) (c's grade) EQUALS JUST (c's pay)))
                                 (r's `the row's cells`)))
                (a's `annexed pay table's rows`))

-- (1) A cell by the steps a table prints: its header's rise to the grade
-- (the product of every grade step at or below it), and the steps printed
-- beside its rows down to the row; at an intermediate grade, the mean of
-- the two grades beside it (§46(א)'s "דרגות ביניים", printed halfway).
GIVEN t IS AN `annexed pay table`, g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the header's rise to grade` t g IS
    product (map (GIVEN s YIELD 1 PLUS s's `the rate of the step`)
                 (filter (GIVEN s YIELD s's `the grade the step reaches` AT MOST g) (t's `annexed pay table's grade steps`)))

GIVEN t IS AN `annexed pay table`, l IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the steps printed down to` t l IS
    catMaybes (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the row's printed step`)
                   (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the row's label` AT MOST l) (t's `annexed pay table's rows`)))

GIVEN whole IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `at the grade or halfway between` whole g IS
    IF FLOOR g EQUALS g
    THEN whole g
    ELSE (whole (g MINUS 0.5) PLUS whole (g PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 2

-- A teachers' cell: a base raised by every seniority step down to the row
-- and every grade step up to the grade.
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER, t IS AN `annexed pay table`, l IS A NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a teachers' cell by the printed steps from` base t l g IS
    `at the grade or halfway between` (GIVEN x YIELD base TIMES product (map (GIVEN s YIELD 1 PLUS s) (`the steps printed down to` t l)) TIMES `the header's rise to grade` t x) g

-- A principals' cell: a base raised by the grade steps, with the shekels
-- printed beside every level up to the row.
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER, t IS AN `annexed pay table`, l IS A NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a principals' cell by the printed steps from` base t l g IS
    `at the grade or halfway between` (GIVEN x YIELD (base TIMES `the header's rise to grade` t x) PLUS sum (`the steps printed down to` t l)) g

-- §35(א) and §46(ג): the tables are of 1.12.2008, and the first-degree
-- table starts at 5,379.5, §46(ג)'s least table pay at seniority 0 in the
-- December 2008 salary.
`the first-degree base` MEANS `the least table pay at seniority 0` `the annexed salary tables are updated from`

#ASSERT `the annexed salary tables are updated from` EQUALS `the tables are as of`
#ASSERT `annexes ד and ה as this copy prints them` `the first-degree table` 1 0 EQUALS JUST `the first-degree base`
#ASSERT `the first-degree base` EQUALS 5379.5

-- Every cell of annexes ד' and ו' is that base raised by the steps the
-- table prints, rounded once.
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise than` `this copy's annex ד'` (GIVEN l, g YIELD `a teachers' cell by the printed steps from` `the first-degree base` `this copy's annex ד'` l g))
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise than` `this copy's annex ו'` (GIVEN l, g YIELD `a teachers' cell by the printed steps from` `the first-degree base` `this copy's annex ו'` l g))

-- No clause says how the other teachers' tables stand to the first-degree
-- one. Their cells show the second-degree tables (ה', ז') at 105% of its
-- base and the senior certified teachers' (ט') at 75%, each rounded once;
-- the certified and uncertified teachers' (י', י"א) at no such share of a
-- printed figure — their steps are checked below.
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise than` `this copy's annex ה'` (GIVEN l, g YIELD `a teachers' cell by the printed steps from` (105% TIMES `the first-degree base`) `this copy's annex ה'` l g))
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise than` `this copy's annex ז'` (GIVEN l, g YIELD `a teachers' cell by the printed steps from` (105% TIMES `the first-degree base`) `this copy's annex ז'` l g))
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise than` `this copy's annex ט'` (GIVEN l, g YIELD `a teachers' cell by the printed steps from` (75% TIMES `the first-degree base`) `this copy's annex ט'` l g))

-- §46(א): the conversion tables are the salary tables with intermediate
-- grades — every cell ד' prints, ו' prints at the same place, and ה''s, ז'.
#ASSERT null (`the cells one table prints otherwise than the other` `this copy's annex ד'` `this copy's annex ו'`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells one table prints otherwise than the other` `this copy's annex ה'` `this copy's annex ז'`)

-- §38(ב): the first seniority at which annexes ד' and ה' print a grade is
-- the years §38(ב) asks in each grade below it, added up from grade 1 at
-- seniority 0.
GIVEN t IS AN `annexed pay table`, g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the first seniority printing grade` t g IS
    listToMaybe (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the row's label`)
                     (filter (GIVEN r YIELD any (GIVEN c YIELD c's grade EQUALS g) (r's `the row's cells`)) (t's `annexed pay table's rows`)))

#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD `the first seniority printing grade` `this copy's annex ד'` g EQUALS JUST (sum (map `years in the grade below for promotion to` (range 2 g)))) (range 2 9)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD `the first seniority printing grade` `this copy's annex ה'` g EQUALS JUST (sum (map `years in the grade below for promotion to` (range 2 g)))) (range 2 9)

-- The teachers' tables at work. §47(ג)(3)'s 8,625.22 is annex ו' at
-- seniority 16, grade 4.5. §46(ב): §61's example places A = 7,480 on
-- annex ו' at seniority 18 at grade 2.5, 7,613.70 (the example prints
-- 7,614). §46(ה): a second-degree teacher with A = 8,190 at seniority 15
-- takes the grade the first-degree row gives, 4, on annex ז'. §56: §61's
-- example places A = 6,248 on annex ט' at seniority 15 at grade 4.5,
-- 6,404.87 (printed 6,405). A row the corpus cannot read in full gives no
-- placement.
#ASSERT `the annexed pay at` `this copy's annex ו'` 16 4.5 EQUALS JUST 8625.22
#ASSERT `the placement in the row` 7480 (fromMaybe EMPTY (`the row of annex ו or ז for the seniority` `the first-degree table` 18)) EQUALS JUST (`cell` 2.5 7613.70)
#ASSERT `to the nearest whole` 7613.70 EQUALS 7614
#ASSERT `the placement after conversion` `a second degree` 8190 (fromMaybe EMPTY (`the row of annex ו or ז for the seniority` `the first-degree table` 15)) (fromMaybe EMPTY (`the row of annex ו or ז for the seniority` `the second-degree table` 15)) EQUALS JUST (`cell` 4 8642.71)
#ASSERT `a non-academic's placement` 6248 (fromMaybe EMPTY (`the row of the rank's table for the seniority` `a senior certified teacher` 15)) EQUALS JUST (`cell` 4.5 6404.87)
#ASSERT `the row of the rank's table for the seniority` `a certified teacher` 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the row of the rank's table for the seniority` `a certified teacher` 34 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT isJust (`the row of the rank's table for the seniority` `a certified teacher` 33)
#ASSERT isJust (`the row of the rank's table for the seniority` `an uncertified teacher or instructor` 34)
#ASSERT `annexes ט to י"א as this copy prints them` `the certified teachers' table (annex י')` 0 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `annexes ט to י"א as this copy prints them` `the certified teachers' table (annex י')` 0 1.5 EQUALS JUST 3815.66
#ASSERT `annexes ד and ה as this copy prints them` `the second-degree table` 9 21 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `annexes ד and ה as this copy prints them` `the second-degree table` 9 22 EQUALS JUST 13677.47

-- F-ofek-hadash-base-registry-copy-f: §61's example says its figures are
-- the annexed tables' ("לשם הפשטות נלקחו הערכים בדוגמא זו רק מטבלאות השכר
-- החדשות והמעודכנות, כפי שהן מופיעות בנספחים"), and prints them to the
-- shekel. Of the nine it reads off annex ט', seven are the table's cell to
-- the shekel; two are not — 6,468 for seniority 16, grade 4.5 (the table:
-- 6,468.91) and 6,838 for seniority 18, grade 5 (6,837.46), which the
-- example uses twice. The reading adopted: the table governs (convention
-- precedence.table); the example's arrears of 235, 239 and 512 are an
-- illustration.
@desc A cell of annex ט' §61's example reads, and the figure it prints for it.
DECLARE `figure §61's example reads` HAS
    `the cell it reads`    IS AN `annexed cell`
    `the figure it prints` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN l IS A NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `figure §61's example reads`
DECIDE `§61's example reads` l g f IS
    `figure §61's example reads` WITH
        `the cell it reads`    IS `the annexed cell at` l g
        `the figure it prints` IS f

`the figures §61's example reads off annex ט'` MEANS LIST
    `§61's example reads` 15 4.5 6405, `§61's example reads` 15 5 6636,
    `§61's example reads` 16 5 6703, `§61's example reads` 16 4.5 6468,
    `§61's example reads` 17 5 6770, `§61's example reads` 17 4.5 6534,
    `§61's example reads` 18 5 6838, `§61's example reads` 18 4.5 6599,
    `§61's example reads` 18 6 7350

GIVEN x IS A `figure §61's example reads`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the example's figure is the cell to the shekel` x IF
    CONSIDER `the annexed pay at` `this copy's annex ט'` (x's `the cell it reads`'s `the cell's label`) (x's `the cell it reads`'s `the cell's grade`)
    WHEN JUST p THEN `to the nearest whole` p EQUALS x's `the figure it prints`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

`§61's example reads two cells of annex ט' otherwise` MEANS
    map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `the cell it reads`)
        (filter (GIVEN x YIELD NOT `the example's figure is the cell to the shekel` x) `the figures §61's example reads off annex ט'`)
    EQUALS LIST (`the annexed cell at` 16 4.5), (`the annexed cell at` 18 5)
#ASSERT `§61's example reads two cells of annex ט' otherwise`
#ASSERT `annexes ט to י"א as this copy prints them` `the senior certified teachers' table (annex ט')` 16 4.5 EQUALS JUST 6468.91
#ASSERT `annexes ט to י"א as this copy prints them` `the senior certified teachers' table (annex ט')` 18 5 EQUALS JUST 6837.46

-- §65(ב): the principals' table starts at 12,383, the least pay of a
-- grade-1 principal in the December 2008 salary; §67's examples'
-- supplements, 1,218 a level and 2,436 at level 3, are the shekels the
-- table prints beside its levels.
`the principals' base` MEANS `a grade-1 principal's least pay` `the annexed salary tables are updated from`

#ASSERT `annex י"ב as this copy prints it` 1 1 EQUALS JUST `the principals' base`
#ASSERT `the principals' base` EQUALS 12383
#ASSERT `the steps printed down to` `this copy's annex י"ב` 4 EQUALS LIST 1218, 1218, 1218
#ASSERT sum (`the steps printed down to` `this copy's annex י"ב` 3) EQUALS 2436

-- Every cell of annexes י"ב and י"ג is 12,383 raised by the header's 8.75%
-- a grade, with 1,218 a level, rounded once; and §92(א), §98(ב): every
-- cell of annexes י"ז and י"ח is 75% of the principals' cell so made,
-- rounded once.
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise than` `this copy's annex י"ב` (GIVEN l, g YIELD `a principals' cell by the printed steps from` `the principals' base` `this copy's annex י"ב` l g))
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise than` `this copy's annex י"ג` (GIVEN l, g YIELD `a principals' cell by the printed steps from` `the principals' base` `this copy's annex י"ג` l g))
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise than` `this copy's annex י"ז` (GIVEN l, g YIELD `the first deputies' share of the principals' table` TIMES `a principals' cell by the printed steps from` `the principals' base` `this copy's annex י"ב` l g))
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise than` `this copy's annex י"ח` (GIVEN l, g YIELD `the first deputies' share of the principals' table` TIMES `a principals' cell by the printed steps from` `the principals' base` `this copy's annex י"ג` l g))

-- §§71(א), 98(ב): the salary tables inside their conversion tables. And
-- the senior certified principals' conversion table (י"ד) prints the
-- academic first deputies' conversion cells (י"ח), cell for cell: no rule
-- asks it, and none forbids it.
#ASSERT null (`the cells one table prints otherwise than the other` `this copy's annex י"ב` `this copy's annex י"ג`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells one table prints otherwise than the other` `this copy's annex י"ז` `this copy's annex י"ח`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells one table prints otherwise than the other` `this copy's annex י"ד` `this copy's annex י"ח`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells one table prints otherwise than the other` `this copy's annex י"ח` `this copy's annex י"ד`)

-- The principals' and deputies' tables at work. §74's example: A = 14,375
-- on annex י"ג at level 3 is placed at grade 1, 14,819. §87's: A = 11,200
-- on annex י"ד at level 3 at grade 1.5, 11,520.57 (printed 11,521); grade
-- 2 there, 11,926.88, with the example's 16.6%, is its 13,907; and A =
-- 13,130 on annex י"ג at level 3 at grade 1, 14,819. §98 and §109 on a
-- row of annexes י"ח and כ'.
#ASSERT `a principal's placement` 14375 (fromMaybe EMPTY (`the row of annex י"ג for the level` 3)) EQUALS JUST (`cell` 1 14819)
#ASSERT `a non-academic principal's placement` 11200 (`the cells of the row labelled` (`this copy's non-academic principals' table for` (`the principals' table for the rank` `a senior certified teacher's rank`)) 3) EQUALS JUST (`cell` 1.5 11520.57)
#ASSERT `to the nearest whole` 11520.57 EQUALS 11521
#ASSERT `annexes י"ד to ט"ז as this copy prints them` `the senior certified principals' table (annex י"ד)` 3 2 EQUALS JUST 11926.88
#ASSERT `to the nearest whole` (11926.88 TIMES 1.166) EQUALS 13907
#ASSERT `a principal's placement` 13130 (fromMaybe EMPTY (`the row of annex י"ג for the level` 3)) EQUALS JUST (`cell` 1 14819)
#ASSERT `a first deputy's placement` 12000 (fromMaybe EMPTY (`the row of annex י"ח for the level` 3)) EQUALS JUST (`cell` 2.5 12368.75)
#ASSERT `a non-academic first deputy's placement` 8000 (`the cells of the row labelled` (`this copy's non-academic first deputies' table for` (`the first deputies' table for the rank` `a certified first deputy`)) 2) EQUALS JUST (`cell` 3 8132.87)
#ASSERT `annexes י"ט to כ"א as this copy prints them` `the uncertified first deputies' table (annex כ"א)` 4 4 EQUALS JUST 8734.75

-- (2) The steps each table prints, set beside its cells: a teachers' row's
-- rise over the row above (2%, then 1%), a header's rise of each grade over
-- the grade before it (7.5% and 8.5%, a principal's 8.75%) in a row that
-- does not rise in shekels, a principals' or deputies' level's rise in
-- shekels over the level below, and an intermediate grade as the mean of
-- the grades beside it.
@desc Which printed step a check sets beside a cell.
DECLARE `kind of printed step` IS ONE OF
    `a seniority step`
    `a level step in shekels`
    `a grade step`
    `an intermediate grade`

@desc A cell set beside what a printed step makes of its neighbours: the agorot the printed cell is above (or, negative, below) it.
DECLARE `annexed step check` HAS
    `the cell checked`     IS AN `annexed cell`
    `the step checked`     IS A `kind of printed step`
    `the agorot it is off` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN k IS A `kind of printed step`, l IS A NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER, printed IS A NUMBER, made IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `annexed step check`
DECIDE `a step check of` k l g printed made IS
    `annexed step check` WITH
        `the cell checked`     IS `the annexed cell at` l g
        `the step checked`     IS k
        `the agorot it is off` IS (printed MINUS made) TIMES 100

GIVEN t IS AN `annexed pay table`, r IS AN `annexed pay row`, c IS A `grade cell`
GIVETH A LIST OF `annexed step check`
DECIDE `the row step check of the cell` t r c IS
    CONSIDER r's `the row's printed step`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
    WHEN JUST s THEN
        CONSIDER `the annexed pay at` t (r's `the row's label` MINUS 1) (c's grade)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
        WHEN JUST before THEN
            IF t's `annexed pay table's rows are` EQUALS `rows of seniority for pay`
            THEN LIST (`a step check of` `a seniority step` (r's `the row's label`) (c's grade) (c's pay) (`to the agora` (before TIMES (1 PLUS s))))
            ELSE LIST (`a step check of` `a level step in shekels` (r's `the row's label`) (c's grade) (c's pay) (before PLUS s))

GIVEN t IS AN `annexed pay table`, r IS AN `annexed pay row`, c IS A `grade cell`
GIVETH A LIST OF `annexed step check`
DECIDE `the grade step check of the cell` t r c IS
    IF isJust (r's `the row's printed step`) AND t's `annexed pay table's rows are` EQUALS `rows of complexity level`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE CONSIDER filter (GIVEN st YIELD st's `the grade the step reaches` EQUALS c's grade) (t's `annexed pay table's grade steps`)
         WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
         WHEN st FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
             CONSIDER `the annexed pay at` t (r's `the row's label`) (c's grade MINUS 1)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
             WHEN JUST before THEN LIST (`a step check of` `a grade step` (r's `the row's label`) (c's grade) (c's pay) (`to the agora` (before TIMES (1 PLUS st's `the rate of the step`))))

GIVEN t IS AN `annexed pay table`, r IS AN `annexed pay row`, c IS A `grade cell`
GIVETH A LIST OF `annexed step check`
DECIDE `the intermediate grade check of the cell` t r c IS
    IF FLOOR (c's grade) EQUALS c's grade
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE CONSIDER `the annexed pay at` t (r's `the row's label`) (c's grade MINUS 0.5)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
         WHEN JUST below THEN
             CONSIDER `the annexed pay at` t (r's `the row's label`) (c's grade PLUS 0.5)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
             WHEN JUST above THEN LIST (`a step check of` `an intermediate grade` (r's `the row's label`) (c's grade) (c's pay) (`to the agora` ((below PLUS above) DIVIDED BY 2)))

GIVEN t IS AN `annexed pay table`
GIVETH A LIST OF `annexed step check`
DECIDE `the step checks of` t IS
    concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD
                     concat (map (GIVEN c YIELD concat (LIST `the row step check of the cell` t r c, `the grade step check of the cell` t r c, `the intermediate grade check of the cell` t r c))
                                 (r's `the row's cells`)))
                (t's `annexed pay table's rows`))

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, cs IS A LIST OF `annexed step check`
GIVETH A LIST OF `annexed step check`
DECIDE `the checks more than` n `agorot off among` cs IS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the agorot it is off` GREATER THAN n OR c's `the agorot it is off` LESS THAN (0 MINUS n)) cs

GIVEN t IS AN `annexed pay table`
GIVETH A LIST OF `annexed step check`
DECIDE `the level steps of` t IS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the step checked` EQUALS `a level step in shekels`) (`the step checks of` t)

GIVEN t IS AN `annexed pay table`
GIVETH A LIST OF `annexed step check`
DECIDE `the percentage and intermediate steps of` t IS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD NOT (c's `the step checked` EQUALS `a level step in shekels`)) (`the step checks of` t)

-- Every rate a table prints makes each cell from its printed neighbour to
-- within an agora (the cells are rounded once, from a base, not one from
-- another), and so does every intermediate grade.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD null (`the checks more than` 1 `agorot off among` (`the step checks of` t))) `this copy's teachers' salary tables`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD null (`the checks more than` 1 `agorot off among` (`the percentage and intermediate steps of` t))) `this copy's principals' and deputies' tables`

-- F-ofek-hadash-base-registry-copy-g: the shekels printed beside the
-- levels. The academic principals' tables (י"ב, י"ג) print "₪ 1,218" and
-- their levels rise by exactly 1,218. Every other principals' and deputies'
-- table prints a whole number of shekels its levels do not rise by, each
-- the true rise rounded to the shekel: the first deputies' "₪ 914" over a
-- rise of 913.50 — 75% of 1,218, as §92(א) derives them — and the
-- non-academic tables' 914, 833, 724, 685, 624 and 543 likewise. A first
-- deputy's or a non-academic principal's complexity supplement on a fall of
-- level (§67(ד), applied by §§82, 93 and 111) turns on which is the
-- supplement. The reading adopted: the cells govern, and the supplement is
-- the rise between them (convention rounding.printed-figure: the printed
-- cell is the rule).
`the shekels printed beside the levels are the rise rounded` MEANS
        all (GIVEN t YIELD null (`the checks more than` 0 `agorot off among` (`the level steps of` t))) `this copy's academic principals' tables`
    AND all (GIVEN t YIELD
                     all (GIVEN c YIELD NOT (c's `the agorot it is off` EQUALS 0)) (`the level steps of` t)
                 AND null (`the checks more than` 50 `agorot off among` (`the level steps of` t)))
            `this copy's other principals' and deputies' tables`
    AND `the steps printed down to` `this copy's annex י"ז` 2 EQUALS LIST 914
    AND `the first deputies' share of the principals' table` TIMES 1218 EQUALS 913.5
    AND `annex י"ב as this copy prints it` 1 1 EQUALS JUST 12383
    AND `the annexed pay at` `this copy's annex י"ז` 2 1 EQUALS JUST 10200.75
    AND `the annexed pay at` `this copy's annex י"ז` 1 1 EQUALS JUST 9287.25
#ASSERT `the shekels printed beside the levels are the rise rounded`
#ASSERT count (`the level steps of` `this copy's annex י"ז`) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT count (`the level steps of` `this copy's annex י"ח`) EQUALS 21

-- The reading, at work: a level's complexity supplement on a table is the
-- rise of its cells over level 1 — the same at every grade — and
-- that is what §67(ד) reads on a fall, for a first deputy by §93 "בהתאם
-- לטבלת השכר המשולב של סגני המנהלים הראשונים": 913.50 a level, 1,827 at
-- level 3. Four years at level 3, then level 2: 4 × 10% × 1,827 + 60% ×
-- 913.50 = 1,278.90.
GIVEN t IS AN `annexed pay table`, l IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the complexity supplement of the level on` t l IS
    CONSIDER `the annexed pay at` t l 1
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST here THEN
        CONSIDER `the annexed pay at` t 1 1
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST first THEN JUST (here MINUS first)

#ASSERT `the complexity supplement of the level on` `this copy's annex י"ב` 2 EQUALS JUST 1218
#ASSERT `the complexity supplement of the level on` `this copy's annex י"ב` 3 EQUALS JUST 2436
#ASSERT `the complexity supplement of the level on` `this copy's annex י"ז` 2 EQUALS JUST 913.5
#ASSERT `the complexity supplement of the level on` `this copy's annex י"ז` 3 EQUALS JUST 1827
#ASSERT `the supplement after a fall` (replicate 4 1827) 913.5 EQUALS 1278.9

-- (3) Every table rises along its grades and down its rows, so "the grade
-- nearest at or above A" (§46(ב), §71(ב)) is one cell.
GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `grade cell`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row rises along its grades` cs IF
    and (zipWith (GIVEN x, y YIELD x's grade LESS THAN y's grade AND x's pay LESS THAN y's pay) cs (drop 1 cs))

GIVEN t IS AN `annexed pay table`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the table rises along its grades and down its rows` t IF
        all (GIVEN r YIELD `the row rises along its grades` (r's `the row's cells`)) (t's `annexed pay table's rows`)
    AND all (GIVEN r YIELD all (GIVEN c YIELD
                                    CONSIDER `the annexed pay at` t (r's `the row's label` MINUS 1) (c's grade)
                                    WHEN JUST above THEN above LESS THAN c's pay
                                    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)
                               (r's `the row's cells`))
            (t's `annexed pay table's rows`)

#ASSERT all `the table rises along its grades and down its rows` (append `this copy's teachers' salary tables` `this copy's principals' and deputies' tables`)
#ASSERT count (append `this copy's teachers' salary tables` `this copy's principals' and deputies' tables`) EQUALS 17
